package m08core044transport
    provides [checks, expected_vector, observe, case_body, descriptor, context, check, check_ref, expected_check, evidence, observation, failed, test_case]
    uses [text]

/// M08 CORE-044 "bundled transport loopback: staged suite semantics".
/// Source: tests/integration/transport_test.go symbol
/// TestBundledTransportLoopback (L13-38).
/// Related fixtures: the seven staged runtime suites (Go L26):
/// runtime/test/transport-request.test.ts (request prep + snapshots),
/// runtime/test/transport-body.test.ts (caps + deadlines),
/// runtime/test/transport-owned.test.ts (owned continuations),
/// runtime/test/transport-fetch.test.ts (raw fetch loopback),
/// runtime/test/transport-http.test.ts (nominal catalogue errors),
/// runtime/test/transport-named.test.ts (named fetch + media),
/// runtime/test/transport-late.test.ts (late faults).
/// Disposition: RETAIN (migrate row; the old Go harness stays until the
/// integrator retires it after every linked row, variant, environment and
/// control has accepted evidence).
/// Protects (this file): request preparation validates URLs, auth and
/// headers before launch while preserving duplicate cookies and normalizing
/// fields; raw and named fetch observe exact bodies, media/charset,
/// redirects, timeout/cancellation phases, byte caps and nominal transport
/// errors; owned continuations drain and retain resources while late
/// decoder/transport faults preserve the chosen timeout and report
/// diagnostics correctly.
/// The roots-green pin lives in core-044-roots-green.can; the production
/// process shape lives in core-044-run-shape.can.
/// Variants: one-attempt (fetch-one-attempt), stalled body (body-stall,
/// fetch-stall), redirect (fetch-redirect), malformed reply (named-prefail),
/// late fault (late-timeout-kept, late-retains, late-classified-silent).
/// All seven suites are represented: request 6, body 2, owned 2, fetch 5,
/// http 2, named 4, late 3 checks.
/// Environment: CAN_BUN_ARCHIVE + macOS sandbox-exec + localhost
/// bind/outbound; requires can-bun-archive, macos-sandbox-exec. Logical
/// gates SUITE/WORK/PROC and C/R/N/S/A identities bind at P23/QHTTP; no
/// live run now. Descriptor timeout 120000ms mirrors the Go 2-minute ctx (L19).
/// Delegated oracles: DELEGATE-023 through DELEGATE-029 recorded on the
/// roots slice; read-only record, not executed here.
/// Execution credit: NOT claimed (accept_after P23/QHTTP unmet).
/// Case transport/loopback-semantics checks: prep-encoding, prep-auth,
/// prep-url-guards, prep-secret-safe, snapshot-cookies, snapshot-combined,
/// body-cap, body-stall, owned-retains, owned-drains, fetch-one-attempt,
/// fetch-redirect, fetch-stall, fetch-cancel-phase, fetch-cap, http-nominal,
/// http-status, named-media, named-json, named-envelope, named-prefail,
/// late-timeout-kept, late-retains, late-classified-silent.
/// Facet map (fixture legs): prep-encoding pins native URL query encoding
/// (transport-request.test.ts L26: the items URL with "a_b=a+b&a_b=%2B%25&"
/// + "a_b=" verbatim); prep-auth pins passthrough auth (L28: "Bearer secret"
/// with one credential read, L29); prep-url-guards pins the
/// five invalid URL shapes failing before any credential read (L32-37:
/// origin/path_query/fragment/userinfo/url; reads 0 at L49); prep-secret-safe
/// pins disclosure-free credential/header failures (L52-86: credential/
/// credential_value/header_name/header_value problems; cause is exactly
/// "Error: Can transport failure" at L63; header-value reads 0 at L85);
/// snapshot-cookies pins duplicate cookie preservation (L95-96: two
/// separate set-cookie entries); snapshot-combined pins normalized combined
/// fields (L97: "one, two"); body-cap pins the byte cap
/// (transport-body.test.ts L18-25: limit 3 rejects the first excessive
/// chunk and cancels the stream); body-stall pins the stalled-body bound
/// (L29-49: 20ms deadline, stream cancelled); owned-retains pins work
/// retention past the deadline verdict (transport-owned.test.ts L40-42:
/// done false until native settles, then ok); owned-drains pins
/// continuation draining (L94-95: ok with the resource used);
/// fetch-one-attempt pins a single attempt per request with no cookie jar
/// (transport-fetch.test.ts L61-63: two requests, two attempts, null
/// cookies, redacted auth); fetch-redirect pins manual 302 handling
/// (L93-108: status 302 returned or observed, decoder never entered);
/// fetch-stall pins the stalled-response timeout (L144-149: 30ms, one
/// attempt, decode never entered); fetch-cancel-phase pins the exact
/// cancellation phase (L205: "cancelled"); fetch-cap pins the 50-byte
/// bound (L246-249: outgoing overflow prevents the credential read and
/// the launch; L265-271: decompressed overflow rejected after one
/// attempt); http-nominal pins the four nominal catalogue occurrences
/// (transport-http.test.ts L85-122: invalid_request/origin,
/// credentials_missing/TOKEN, body_limit/3, transport_failed/connect);
/// http-status pins typed status payloads (L144-150: status_error 401);
/// named-media pins strict media/charset validation
/// (transport-named.test.ts L146-156: seven malformed shapes rejected);
/// named-json pins exact bigint decode (L175/L206: count 9007199254740993);
/// named-envelope pins the immutable 418 envelope (L230-237: status 418,
/// exact bytes, duplicate cookies, folded x-repeat); named-prefail pins
/// pre-launch failure mapping (L359-408: utf8/charset/invalid_json/
/// media_type/duplicate_member/content_type/unicode_scalar/limit reasons
/// with zero launches past the gate); late-timeout-kept pins timeout
/// selection under a late defect (transport-late.test.ts L54-66: 2000ms
/// timeout kept, late native_exception diagnostic); late-retains pins
/// resource retention past a parent timeout (L133-134: never prematurely
/// closed, still used); late-classified-silent pins silent late classified
/// faults (L168: diagnostics stay []).
/// Shared old files untouched; retirement is a later integrator decision.
record context
    str case_id
    str variant_id
    str workspace
    str run_id
record check
    str id
    str title
record check_ref
    str id
record expected_check
    str check
    str expected
record evidence
    str check
    str expected
    str observed
    bool matched
    str selector
record observation
    str prep_encoding
    str prep_auth
    int prep_url_guards
    bool prep_secret_safe
    int snapshot_cookies
    str snapshot_combined
    int body_cap
    int body_stall
    bool owned_retains
    bool owned_drains
    bool fetch_one_attempt
    int fetch_redirect
    int fetch_stall
    str fetch_cancel_phase
    int fetch_cap
    int http_nominal
    int http_status
    int named_media
    int named_json
    int named_envelope
    bool named_prefail
    int late_timeout_kept
    bool late_retains
    bool late_classified_silent
error failed{str check}
record test_case
    str id
    str[] tags
    str[] requires
    int timeout_ms
    check_ref[] required_checks
    callable void (context) emits {failed} body
fn str selector
    emits {}
    given
        context c
        str root
    asserts
        sample: context("transport/loopback-semantics", "default", "", "offline"), "prep-encoding" => ok "case transport/loopback-semantics variant default root prep-encoding run offline"
    ok call text::join(["case", c.case_id, "variant", c.variant_id, "root", root, "run", c.run_id], " ")
fn evidence require_bool
    emits {failed}
    given
        bool observed
        bool expected
        context c
        str check
    asserts
        same: true, true, context("transport/loopback-semantics", "default", "", "offline"), "prep-secret-safe" => ok evidence("prep-secret-safe", "true", "true", true, "case transport/loopback-semantics variant default root prep-secret-safe run offline")
        different: false, true, context("transport/loopback-semantics", "default", "", "offline"), "prep-secret-safe" => failed{"prep-secret-safe"}
    match observed is expected
        false => failed{check}
        true => ok evidence(check, call text::from_bool(expected), call text::from_bool(observed), true, call selector(c, check))
fn evidence require_int
    emits {failed}
    given
        int observed
        int expected
        context c
        str check
    asserts
        same: 5, 5, context("transport/loopback-semantics", "default", "", "offline"), "prep-url-guards" => ok evidence("prep-url-guards", "5", "5", true, "case transport/loopback-semantics variant default root prep-url-guards run offline")
        different: 4, 5, context("transport/loopback-semantics", "default", "", "offline"), "prep-url-guards" => failed{"prep-url-guards"}
    match observed is expected
        false => failed{check}
        true => ok evidence(check, call text::from_int(expected), call text::from_int(observed), true, call selector(c, check))
fn evidence require_text
    emits {failed}
    given
        str observed
        str expected
        context c
        str check
    asserts
        same: "https://example.test/api/items?a_b=a+b&a_b=%2B%25&a_b=", "https://example.test/api/items?a_b=a+b&a_b=%2B%25&a_b=", context("transport/loopback-semantics", "default", "", "offline"), "prep-encoding" => ok evidence("prep-encoding", "https://example.test/api/items?a_b=a+b&a_b=%2B%25&a_b=", "https://example.test/api/items?a_b=a+b&a_b=%2B%25&a_b=", true, "case transport/loopback-semantics variant default root prep-encoding run offline")
        different: "https://example.test/api/item?a_b=a+b&a_b=%2B%25&a_b=", "https://example.test/api/items?a_b=a+b&a_b=%2B%25&a_b=", context("transport/loopback-semantics", "default", "", "offline"), "prep-encoding" => failed{"prep-encoding"}
    match observed is expected
        false => failed{check}
        true => ok evidence(check, expected, observed, true, call selector(c, check))
